"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3015021","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b908d19b5951424613dd685e8a91e4aed2abc328041a55121416f13a9ab61ccb","compact":"6d9c664df245dbd4e3e55c0c42184f7a2e88cc2677a300deafa0a1bdbbd04869","nasal":"cacff26600058decab9f865215037f87edf1e99e8898dac1a5a732a637ace609"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-15-22","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":15,"verse":22,"english":"And the streams appear with their waters enveloped in vapour and the cranes, perceived through their cries, and their banks having their sands wet.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.691,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-16-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3015022","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"830edd34ff95f6752c018cdb3a96c4ba0ec77a571180f8fb295c0c684543fc43","compact":"73be287d92340484e00cc6331ccb58141090996a544cbca837a59cafa28ecc7b","nasal":"9f391fdcf3b1d2d5245875a197006994258825f0dc3bd95a50d631a0a5c32f0e"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-15-23","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":15,"verse":23,"english":"What on account of the snow-fall, what of the mildness of the sun, and what through the cold, water even when it is on a mountain top, tastes sweet.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-16-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3015023","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b0ee108fb54f802b2f14a08bca845d9cf702d0178ecf5ca247182f98e20e418d","compact":"5d9944bd8eacdc7438bd8e72510251ba9bdfa80bd563324ec0078e91c4666182","nasal":"5d9944bd8eacdc7438bd8e72510251ba9bdfa80bd563324ec0078e91c4666182"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-15-24","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":15,"verse":24,"english":"And lotuses afflicted by the cold, with the stalks only left, and with their petals dropping down and their pericarps and filaments shrivelled up, do not appear beautiful.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.833,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-16-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3015024","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b5341f889d50386b9d1bf6e0c1c77caac82fa1936b02099b2576ec4ca6e5cb49","compact":"0b396ec705ceff6a6b6a10ca484131f46bae40d1fd13cbbe4ee93f90efeaf1ef","nasal":"27c459a2afef96ebc19b8cbdbb7912b3f686f661571adf579d00513fe16fc181"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-15-25","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":15,"verse":25,"english":"O foremost of men, at this season, influenced by regard for you, Bharata undergoing affliction of spirit, is performing mortification's in the city.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.868,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-16-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3015025","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c35257af7053948977da46edfdede472d8b9faea7f195f6725d38df23e7846f5","compact":"c7e7fda7963f754ce8bf7b074edad82868f9cd338db23338d8a2255a48c42287","nasal":"c7e7fda7963f754ce8bf7b074edad82868f9cd338db23338d8a2255a48c42287"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-15-26","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":15,"verse":26,"english":"And forsaking kingdom, and dignity, and the many and various enjoyments, Bharata practising asceticism and restraining himself in respect of food, in this winter lie down on the bare earth.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-16-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3015026","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9589d6b43ecdcb86a4a3715ca2237b5e128d2bdbbcaea3829b6ec8c1dbbbb47a","compact":"a551b20304ad857fb7556b5491e145de7b2251ac094dd13dc3e25d00049b814a","nasal":"57087d81fccce76661062ea4b42f330d80c0f5f19d8aac7a93d798dc20e4dd17"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-15-27","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":15,"verse":27,"english":"He also for certain, at this hour of the day, surrounded by this subjects, daily wend to the river Sarayū for performing his ablutions.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-16-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3015027","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0a5be9eb1070d0cf1d6706274b9408bbf7ce3ae5851b360412dc5353127d6e75","compact":"2781e2a0dadb89eaea06d61e6a6e07bb726d08fe418047b737b3495b14965ef7","nasal":"2781e2a0dadb89eaea06d61e6a6e07bb726d08fe418047b737b3495b14965ef7"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-15-28","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":15,"verse":28,"english":"Brought up in luxury, and exceedingly tender, how can he, afflicted with cold, perforim his ablutions in the Sarayū during the latter part of the night?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.839,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-16-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3015028","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cce019f767f91d1a998fed0d98b48ddb309f5d399c993729e495df4b064b0f00","compact":"7b0608b0ec14b394b2025476fc67c4d951f70e9dfeb78d621ee8bc0758cb1317","nasal":"e12febf2c2925285f5a30aab7069482b0a480ddef17a399abe7be7b37e3a4a05"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-15-29","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":15,"verse":29,"english":"Of eyes resembling lotus petals, grey-hued, endued with grace, with a navel depressed, and mighty, Bharata understand righteousness, is truth-speaking, of restrained senses (in respect of other' wives) and also of subdued senses. And he speak fair, and is sweet-tempered, and longarmed and the vanquisher of foes. And renouncing various pleasures, he has devoted himself to the noble one.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.861,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-16-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3015029","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8b9d313cc86c868d9885bfd043d7d2ed78cadb0d60db69f289ed37f9c9302849","compact":"79a45b643b97af2fda367ebd830cd6372cfd13ce60a6028b00117a92dd77eaa9","nasal":"0a3a8a11b06f830f07110c0b5e5edc062b3581329de8edcced9b7fc108447b55"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-15-30","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":15,"verse":30,"english":"Of eyes resembling lotus petals, grey-hued, endued with grace, with a navel depressed, and mighty, Bharata understand righteousness, is truth-speaking, of restrained senses (in respect of other' wives) and also of subdued senses. And he speak fair, and is sweet-tempered, and longarmed and the vanquisher of foes. And renouncing various pleasures, he has devoted himself to the noble one.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-16-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3015030","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a661354950f15bf601aeef7dcc203e5fc5aa60fdf43e787c607fbb187c09de78","compact":"84afdc365e9ba620887f0f65d28e69a5ba90cd9f4867901bf8ce7ba764061f95","nasal":"84afdc365e9ba620887f0f65d28e69a5ba90cd9f4867901bf8ce7ba764061f95"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-15-31","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":15,"verse":31,"english":"Your high-souled brother has secured heaven, since he, resorting to asceticism, is iinitating you that resident in the woods.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-16-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3015031","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4bd83af6bbf64331d4de692c2600a960e9f248590a64bc08851f0be9ca167de4","compact":"622e7aaccc6fc39cb35f43cafa71cd89217f7962bc1820fffabd4d1c0ff3fb9e","nasal"